# Auto Graphics content scripts

When writing TikTok video or carousel scripts for this project, follow `docs/message-protocol.md`.

## Hard rules

1. First line: `/video` or `/carousel`
2. Body tags are `kind/category` only: `[photos/...]` or `[videos/...]`
3. Categories: `lifestyle`, `broll`, `coding`, `projects` (plus `thumbnails` for carousel cover)
4. Dual text: `headline | subline`
5. Same-slide line breaks: write `\n` inside text (one script line still = one slide)

### /video

- Optional: `hook: text | subline` — **no** library tag
- Body lines: `[videos/category]`

```text
/video
hook: 4 weeks recap | of my journey
I filmed my real desk for 30 days [videos/lifestyle]
Follow for the tools I used [videos/broll]
```

### /carousel

- Required: `thumbnail: text | subline` — **no** library tag (slide 1 from `photos/thumbnails/`)
- Body lines: `[photos/category]` only — never `[videos/...]`

```text
/carousel
thumbnail: 4 weeks recap | of my journey
Desk setup that actually works [photos/lifestyle]
Tools I used every day [photos/projects]
```

## Tag matching

- `coding` — desk, laptop, learning
- `projects` — GitHub, demos, portfolio
- `lifestyle` — life/journey soft beats only
- `broll` — general / no clear desk or project shot

## Outdated (never use)

- Flat tags: `[broll]`, `[hooks]`, `[lifestyle]`, `[coding]`, `[projects]`
- `hook:` on carousels
- Library tags on `hook:` or `thumbnail:` lines

## Content style

When writing educational / tip carousels or videos for this project, also follow `docs/content-style.md` and the project skill `.cursor/skills/auto-graphics-content/SKILL.md`.

- Beginner-clear, not over-technical
- Default how-to shape: outcome hook + numbered steps (`Step 1`, `Step 2`, …)
- Brief headers; put the explanation in the subline
- Use `\n` for same-slide breaks when it helps reading
- Pain-point tips (jobs, AI updates, platforms, free resources)
- Name only large trusted orgs (e.g. Hugging Face, CS50, Google, OpenAI) — not individual creators
- No Unicode arrows / fancy symbols on slides (`→` breaks fonts) — use `Learn, build, repeat` or `A to B`
- If the user only has one library category stocked, tag all body lines with that category
- Do not apply external Jake TikTok journey skills unless the user asks

When the protocol changes, update `docs/message-protocol.md` first, then this rule.  
When content voice, how-to structure, resource-naming, or on-slide font rules change, update `docs/content-style.md` and the project skill first, then this rule.
